# ── Backups ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anchored to repo root + the one real runtime backup-output directory
# (backend/backups/, written by local-backup-storage.provider.ts via
# `path.join(process.cwd(), 'backups')`). Fix (2026-08-07): this was
# previously the unanchored pattern `backups/`, which — because gitignore
# treats a bare directory name with no leading slash as matching that name
# at ANY depth — also silently matched
# frontend/src/app/(platform)/backup/backups/, a real Next.js route
# directory, not a runtime artifact. That page.tsx was never committed, so
# it was never deployed, so POST-backup navigation to /backup/backups
# 404'd in production despite the source existing and looking correct.
# Root-caused from a live "Start Backup click leads to a 404" report.
/backend/backups/

# ── Claude / AI session files ─────────────────────────────────────
.claude/
